WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.369
-Our next guest is a very
talented comedian and actor

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.838
you know
from the film "Fire Island,"

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.472
the Showtime series
"I Love That for You,"

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.741
and the hit podcast
"Las Culturistas."

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.176
His comedy special,

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.244
"Matt Rogers:
Have You Heard of Christmas?",

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:14.080
premieres December 2nd
on Showtime.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.148
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:18.651
-♪ Santa and Jesus ♪

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:22.888
♪ They were best, best friends ♪

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:26.192
♪ They knew each other ♪

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.061
♪ Way back in college
in Bethlehem ♪

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:33.399
♪ They knew each other
like ooh, ooh, ooh ♪

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.936
♪ They were like,
"Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh" ♪

00:00:37.936 --> 00:00:40.907
-Please welcome to the show
Matt Rogers, everybody!

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.909
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:49.482 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:56.088 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:58.625
-Wow.
-I am so happy you're here!

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.092
-I'm very happy to be here.

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.427
-First-time guest on the show.

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.062
Not your first time
in the studio.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.363
-That is correct.

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:06.265
I sat right about in the middle
over there.

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:09.268
We share a love
of the singer Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:10.502
-We do. We do.

00:01:10.502 --> 00:01:12.305
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, we have some fans.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.708
And I did get a friend
to, like, score me tickets

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.510
to your show one time
when she was on.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.678
-Uh-huh.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.145
-It was her "Meaning of Life"
album tour.

00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:21.881
I came. I sat right over there.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:25.385
And you go out into the audience
and do, like, a little Q&amp;A.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.486
-I do, yeah.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.320
-So I thought
I'd be real funny.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.723
And I was like --
I asked a question,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.159
and it was this question.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:37.130
"Hey, Seth,
Team Justin or team Kelly?"

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.932
And you were like, "Kelly."

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.466
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.135
And sort of moved on.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:45.305
And so that was the way
I met Seth Meyers,

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.373
which wasn't necessarily
how I wanted it to go.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.507
This is much --

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.276
-Yeah, let's treat this
like our first.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.845
-Well, I did used to say
on my podcast a bunch,

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.482
"Las Culturistas"
with Bowen Yang,

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:59.219
that you would be a dream person
to bring home to your parents.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.719
-Oh, that's very nice
of you to say.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:02.154
-I always felt that way
about you.

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:04.523
Like, if you brought him home
to meet the parents,

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:06.492
like, it's Seth Meyers.
You know what I mean?

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.627
And then you sort of crushed it.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:11.264
[ Laughter ]
-Give me a chance.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.132
I think I will --
If I ever meet your parents,

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.168
they will be very impressed.
-Exactly. Exactly.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.836
-So, you have
this Christmas special.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.304
-It's true.
-And you actually --

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.439
We were talking through
the commercial break about

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:22.508
the Rockefeller Center Christmas
tree, which is right --

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.578
You have a song about the tree.
-Yeah.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.982
Well, so, some background on me
is I needed to sort of take back

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.551
Rockefeller Center
because I had a --

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:34.988
a screen test for
"Saturday Night Live"

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:38.124
that went sort of one way
for Bowen Yang

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.159
and another way for me.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.061
-So then it kind of
made me sad to come here.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.796
So I was like,
"I'm going to write a song

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.666
about Rockefeller Center that,
like, takes the power back."

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.168
And so I wrote a song
that's sort of about

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.370
what happens when you come here,

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.172
and it's, like, okay.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.808
You know what I mean?
It's like...there's the tree.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.710
-Yeah.
-We see it.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.412
It's definitely big.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:02.348
You know,
if you're a size queen,

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.284
like, we love the tree.

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:06.920
But then
it's kind of just a tree.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.654
-Yeah.
-Then you go to a restaurant,

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.856
and you have a burger.

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:12.591
It's definitely a burger.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:14.360
-Yeah.
-Costs 45 bucks.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.362
-Uh-huh.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.364
-But so it was nice of me to
sort of drag Rockefeller Center

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.166
so that I can come back here
today a king.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.734
-Take the power back.
-Yes.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.402
-Take the power back.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:26.138
-You mentioned --
You mentioned king.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:28.641
Mariah Carey, of course,
the Queen of Christmas.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.543
-Yes. Good segue.
-You actually -- Thank you.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.512
You reached out to her.
-I did.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.680
-With the hopes
that she would anoint you.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.317
-Basically, my special,
"Have You Heard of Christmas?",

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.685
is sort of me trying to join her

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:41.687
in the pantheon
of Christmas royalty.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:43.122
-Of course, yeah.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.158
-So, she's the Queen
of Christmas, as we know,

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:46.525
trademark be damned or not.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.494
Like, she didn't get
that trademarked,

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.095
but that's who she is.
-Yeah.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:52.565
-So I'm trying to become
the Prince of Christmas.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.567
And I thought, like,
let's write her a letter,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.802
try to get the blessing.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.937
Maybe she'll let me
sing one of her songs.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.638
She did not read it.
-Okay.

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:01.440
-I did not hear back from her.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.210
But I hope that if she's
watching, she does read it

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.246
because
there's a good story in there,

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:08.881
which is when
I was in third grade,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.884
I became very obsessed
with her "Butterfly" album.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.485
-Okay.
-So this is like --

00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:15.487
If any members
of the Lambily are here,

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:17.156
which is the Mariah Carey
fan community --

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.558
Okay. Maybe not.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:22.228
You know that the "Butterfly"
album is sort of when

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.029
she, like, discovered
her sexuality.

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:25.364
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:27.399
-And there's a song.
It's track four on "Butterfly."

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.368
It's called "The Roof,"
and it's basically about her

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:33.139
getting sort of, like, intimate
with Derek Jeter on a roof.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.074
-Oh, wow.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:39.011
-And the rain is slowly falling,
and it's a very sexy song.

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:41.046
And I memorized that song,

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:44.250
and during reading free time
in third grade,

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.386
I just wrote out the lyrics
to that song.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:50.289
And it's really --
it's not for a third grader.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.257
-Yeah.

00:04:52.257 --> 00:04:56.329
-And then my teacher was like,
"Please hand in your journals."

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.064
And so I sort of, I guess,
go into, like, a fugue state

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:01.200
and hand in my journal,
and a few days later,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.904
I guess she wasn't in
the Lambily like you guys.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:09.208
And she was like, "Matthew,
your stories are so vivid.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.077
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:15.314
You are beyond your years."

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:18.884
Because I had basically said
everything that could happen

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.786
with Derek Jeter on a roof

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:24.056
besides Derek Jeter,
like, nailed me on a roof.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:25.791
Which would have
been interesting

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:27.226
for my parents to hear about.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.961
-I love -- I love --
-'Cause we were Mets fans.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.330
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]
-Still are.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.632
-You reveal a little --

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:36.368
some biographical details about
Mrs. Claus in your special,

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:38.971
and I feel like not a lot
of people have made an effort

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.306
to tell her story.
-They have not.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.974
-I thought that was
so noble of you.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.275
-Thank you for saying that.

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:46.779
And she has been --
She's been lost to time.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:49.716
You know, she's this character
that we celebrate,

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:51.584
and, you know,
we're trying to draw out,

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.752
like, who this female character
of Christmas is.

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:56.689
And people don't know.
They know she's Mrs. Claus,

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.091
but they don't know
she's actually Kristen.

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:00.659
-Okay.
Oh, that's her first name.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.628
-Kristen Giordano.
-Really?!

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.398
-Yeah.
She came from Syosset, New York.

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.533
[ Applause ]
Yes.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:12.704
And basically I wrote a song in
my special which is sort of --

00:06:12.704 --> 00:06:15.574
It's very much like
a Kelly Clarkson revenge ballad

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:18.043
about what happens when
she finally got a calculator

00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:20.279
and crunched the numbers,
and there's no way her husband

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:22.915
is seeing every home
in 24 hours.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.617
-Yeah.
-So where have you been?

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.284
-Right. Exactly.

00:06:26.284 --> 00:06:30.789
We talk about -- in
"Las Culturistas" with Bowen --

00:06:30.789 --> 00:06:33.325
can you talk about
where Christmas ends?

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:35.961
There's sort of three stages
of pop stardom.

00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:37.463
-Okay. Right.
So basically, like,

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.398
in this special,
"Have You Heard of Christmas?",

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:42.135
this is me in my pop-star era
doing Christmas.

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:43.802
-Okay.
-So every pop star has, like,

00:06:43.802 --> 00:06:46.071
a Christmas era, we all know.

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:47.506
They have two other eras.

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:52.478
There's circus, where a pop star
is sort of in a circus.

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.013
-Okay.

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:57.350
-There's "I'm angry about
surveillance and cameras."

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.818
-Oh, I see.

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:01.820
-Where -- Because of a result of
the success of the circus era.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.623
-Yeah.
-The pop star then has to go

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:06.659
put the cameras away,
like, very --

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:08.127
-Seems very unfair for someone

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.428
who was just in a circus.
-Exactly.

00:07:09.428 --> 00:07:11.029
-You can't be angry if people
are looking at you.

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:12.565
-But that's sort of
the narrative.

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.601
It's like, "I wanted it.
Now I don't want it."

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:18.070
And then when you calm down,
you do your Christmas era,

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.772
which is -- and, of course,

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.974
every pop star really
genuinely loves Christmas,

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.675
and they're not just trying
to make money off the holiday.

00:07:23.675 --> 00:07:26.012
-Of course. They all naturally
come to their first love.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.781
-Exactly.
Everyone, like, is dropped in.

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.482
They know what
they really want to do

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:32.084
is celebrate Christmas
every year.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:34.587
And it's not about money.
It's not about money.

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:35.987
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.987 --> 00:07:39.358
-So, you saw "Titanique,"
which we're going to do next.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.826
You saw the show
and loved the show,

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:42.628
and you're actually going to
help out with the introduction.

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:44.830
-I am. This is -- You guys
are in for a real treat.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.932
"Titanique"
is the best live theater

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:48.834
you can see in New York
right now.

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:50.870
[ Cheers and applause ]
And I'm really excited.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.872
Just a cameo, I'd say.
-Just a cameo.

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:55.975
And one last thing.
That is very exciting.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:57.610
You are also on
"Celebrity Jeopardy!"

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.810
-Yeah, "Jeopardy!" for babies.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.179
-Okay.
"Jeopardy!" for babies.

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:01.447
-Yeah.
-Is it really?

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.181
How much easier would you say
the questions are?

00:08:03.181 --> 00:08:06.152
-It's like,
"Where's America on a map?"

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:10.690
It's literally like,
"Is the ocean blue or red?"

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:13.258
And then you have to, like --
The hard part is the buzzer

00:08:13.258 --> 00:08:15.094
'cause we all know
the ocean's red.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:16.362
-Yeah.

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:17.930
-It's just about being able
to buzz in quickly.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.364
-Right. I've heard from people
it's about --

00:08:19.364 --> 00:08:21.500
You've got to time it
just right.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.801
-Here's the thing.

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:25.771
It's, like, a thick buzzer
with a thick button.

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:28.607
And so if you're like --
You can't negotiate your hand.

00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:30.509
Like, this is me
trying to do it.

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:32.311
-Yeah. So, did you win?

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:34.380
-I came in second place.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.984
John Michael Higgins,
I concede to you.

00:08:38.984 --> 00:08:41.754
And I crushed Aisha Tyler.
She didn't stand a chance.

00:08:41.754 --> 00:08:43.989
-Well, that's very nice. Second
place is quite impressive.

00:08:43.989 --> 00:08:45.424
-Exactly.
-Thank you for being here.

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:46.625
Thank you for sticking around.

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:49.261
"Matt Rogers:
Have You Heard of Christmas?"

00:08:49.261 --> 00:08:51.130
Premieres December 2nd
on Showtime.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.099
We'll be right back
with a performance

00:08:53.099 --> 00:08:55.267
from the cast and musicians
of "Titanique"

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:56.903
with special guest Matt Rogers!

